BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU Bloomington Libraries
DTSTART:20260908T140000Z
DTEND:20260908T150000Z
SUMMARY:AI Literacy
DESCRIPTION:This webinar breaks down what AI literacy actually means: the
  ability to understand\, use\, monitor\, and critically reflect on AI app
 lications with a goal towards understanding how these tools work\, where 
 they fall short\, and how to use them responsibly.We'll cover the basics 
 of AI literacy\, how other literacy frameworks inform AI literacy\, and p
 ractical guidelines for responsible use\, including privacy\, bias\, IU s
 pecific policies\, and knowing whennotto use AI at all. Whether you're ne
 w to AI or already using it regularly\, you'll leave with a clearer frame
 work for AI usage.__________  New to research\, new to managing your own 
 data\, or interested in learning more about research data support at IU? 
 Over the course of the Fall 2026 semester\, join us for webinars designed
  to walk you through the basics of researching with data at IU— from or
 ganizing and storing your data to meeting funder requirements and finding
  the right tools.  Hosted by IU Libraries\, the IU Research Data Commons\
 , and other campus partners\, with sessions useful for researchers at any
  stage. Some sessions may require advanced registration.  For any questio
 ns\, please contact the IU Libraries Research Data Services team (resdata
 @iu.edu (mailto:resdata@iu.edu)) - and don't forget to check back regular
 ly\, as new sessions are added!
