SUMMARY:Teaching Data with ICPSR: Strategies for Success with or without 
 Data
DESCRIPTION:These thoughts go through everyone's heads when incorporating
  something new into their teaching\, but exposing students to social scie
 nce data doesn't have to be onerous. This session will provide an overvie
 w of the topics and types of data available from ICPSR (https://www.icpsr
 .umich.edu/sites/icpsr/home) and give you ideas for including data in cla
 ss\, sometimes without making students touch the data! ICPSR's search too
 ls and the volume of data make it easy to match course concepts with real
 -world examples. We'll also talk about what is and is not acceptable rela
 ted to using ICPSR data in AI. And\, spoiler alert\, you don't have to be
  teaching research methods or statistics to include data!__________  New 
 to research\, new to managing your own data\, or interested in learning m
 ore about research data support at IU? Over the course of the Fall 2026 s
 emester\, join us for webinars designed to walk you through the basics of
  researching with data at IU— from organizing and storing your data to 
 meeting funder requirements and finding the right tools.  Hosted by IU Li
 braries\, the IU Research Data Commons\, and other campus partners\, with
  sessions useful for researchers at any stage. Some sessions may require 
 advanced registration.  For any questions\, please contact the IU Librari
 es Research Data Services team (resdata@iu.edu (mailto:resdata@iu.edu)) -
  and don't forget to check back regularly\, as new sessions are added!
