SUMMARY:Finding and Evaluating Data for Your Research
DESCRIPTION:ICPSR (https://www.icpsr.umich.edu/sites/icpsr/home) is one o
 f the largest archives for social and behavioral science data and\, with 
 over 28\,000 studies\, there might just be something for you! This sessio
 n will introduce you to the kinds of data in ICPSR's holdings\, provide s
 earch tips to help you find what you want\, and describe the standardized
  information (metadata) you can use to evaluate whether the data will wor
 k for your project. We'll talk about how to access both public use data\,
  available with the push of a button or two\, and restricted data._______
 ___  New to research\, new to managing your own data\, or interested in l
 earning more about research data support at IU? Over the course of the Fa
 ll 2026 semester\, join us for webinars designed to walk you through the 
 basics of researching with data at IU— from organizing and storing your
  data to meeting funder requirements and finding the right tools.  Hosted
  by IU Libraries\, the IU Research Data Commons\, and other campus partne
 rs\, with sessions useful for researchers at any stage. Some sessions may
  require advanced registration.  For any questions\, please contact the I
 U Libraries Research Data Services team (resdata@iu.edu (mailto:resdata@i
 u.edu)) - and don't forget to check back regularly\, as new sessions are 
 added!
