DTSTART:20260921T180000Z
DTEND:20260921T190000Z
SUMMARY:Publishing Your Research: Know Your OAptions and Copyrights
DESCRIPTION:Join the Head of the Copyright Program and the Director of Sc
 holarly Communication and Open Publishing for an overview of how copyrigh
 t and publishing choices can affect the visibility\, reuse\, and long-ter
 m impact of your work. We will debunk common copyright myths that can ina
 dvertently limit the reach of your scholarship and explore practical stra
 tegies for increasing research impact through ORCID and IUScholarWorks. W
 hether you are preparing your first article or looking to expand the reac
 h of an established research portfolio\, this workshop will help you make
  informed decisions about sharing and preserving your scholarship._______
 ___  New to research\, new to managing your own data\, or interested in l
 earning more about research data support at IU? Over the course of the Fa
 ll 2026 semester\, join us for webinars designed to walk you through the 
 basics of researching with data at IU— from organizing and storing your
  data to meeting funder requirements and finding the right tools.  Hosted
  by IU Libraries\, the IU Research Data Commons\, and other campus partne
 rs\, with sessions useful for researchers at any stage. Some sessions may
  require advanced registration.  For any questions\, please contact the I
 U Libraries Research Data Services team (resdata@iu.edu (mailto:resdata@i
 u.edu)) - and don't forget to check back regularly\, as new sessions are 
 added!
