SUMMARY:Lecture: The Declaration in a Time of Crisis
DESCRIPTION:We welcome IU Associate Professor of History Konstantin Dierk
 s (https://history.indiana.edu/faculty_staff/faculty/dierks_konstantin.ht
 ml)\, who will give a lecture entitled "The Declaration in a Time of Cris
 is." How do people meet the moment in times of political crisis? The Decl
 aration of Independence tried to meet the crisis of 1776. It pinned blame
  on King George III. It inspired enough colonists to rebel against a migh
 ty empire. It put enduring ideals into American history. The Declaration 
 managed to do so surrounded by a crisis—and before a future—far beyon
 d its grasp. How might we think\, then\, of the issues we face in 2026?  
 Prof. Dierks' talk will be followed by a reception with exhibition curato
 rs and seasonal refreshments. Our friends at the Eskenazi Museum of Art w
 ill be open during this time for interpretive viewings of a Gilbert Stuar
 t portrait of George Washington.  Due to space limitations\, we ask atten
 dees to RSVP for this event.  Event Schedule4:30 p.m.: Konstantin Dierks 
 | Lilly Library Lecture Hall  5:30–6:30 p.m.: Reception | Slocum Room a
 nd Lilly Library galleries  5–7 p.m.: Washington portrait viewing | Esk
 enazi Museum    For more information about visiting the Lilly Library\, i
 ncluding parking and accessibility\, please visit the Lilly Library websi
 te (https://libraries.indiana.edu/signers-opening).
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  We welcome IU Associate Professor of Hi
 story <a href="https://history.indiana.edu/faculty_staff/faculty/dierks_k
 onstantin.html">Konstantin Dierks</a>\, who will give a lecture entitled 
 "The Declaration in a Time of Crisis." How do people meet the moment in t
 imes of political crisis? The Declaration of Independence tried to meet t
 he crisis of 1776. It pinned blame on King George III. It inspired enough
  colonists to rebel against a mighty empire. It put enduring ideals into 
 American history. The Declaration managed to do so surrounded by a crisis
 —and before a future—far beyond its grasp. How might we think\, then\
 , of the issues we face in 2026?</p><p>  Prof. Dierks' talk will be follo
 wed by a reception with exhibition curators and seasonal refreshments. Ou
 r friends at the Eskenazi Museum of Art will be open during this time for
  interpretive viewings of a Gilbert Stuart portrait of George Washington.
 </p><p>  Due to space limitations\, we ask attendees to RSVP for this eve
 nt.</p><h2>  Event Schedule</h2><ul><li data-list-item-id="ea0abef9d79d69
 c3563685c8b98a6a5ba">4:30 p.m.: Konstantin Dierks | Lilly Library Lecture
  Hall  </li><li data-list-item-id="e6f7674d7d5ef9cee183419b5c1873a3e">5:3
 0–6:30 p.m.: Reception | Slocum Room and Lilly Library galleries  </li>
 <li data-list-item-id="e23a7b723761f9a90fe9e9bdf3aa5919c">5–7 p.m.: Was
 hington portrait viewing | Eskenazi Museum  </li></ul><p>  For more infor
 mation about visiting the Lilly Library\, including parking and accessibi
 lity\, please visit <a href="https://libraries.indiana.edu/signers-openin
 g" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the Lilly Library website</a>.</p>
