SUMMARY:You (probably) Haven't Seen This Before - Working Joy
DESCRIPTION:Dive deep into the archival collections of IU Libraries throu
 gh a screening series of rare and unique archival films that center tradi
 tionally underrepresented narratives and underrepresented motion-picture 
 practices\, pushing on and expanding the spectrum of what is considered "
 cinema."  In an effort to keep audiences open-minded and with limited pre
 -conceptions of these rare works of celluloid\, descriptions of films to 
 be shown will not be shared prior to screenings. Join us based on announc
 ed themes and the expectation that the works you see will fall outside of
  Hollywood tropes\, outside of mainstream commercial expectations\, and o
 utside of conventional filmmaking practices. Trust us\, you (probably) ha
 ven't seen these films before!September Program: Working Joy\, curated by
  Addison RogersProgram Description: Working Joy is a concept of taking th
 e necessary break\, the leisure to help get the work done. It's also the 
 necessary work of facilitating good times\, experiences\, true beauty. Se
 lections from IULMIA will take us through the process of enjoying life. G
 oing through the past\, we can see this has always been a practice\, and 
 fortunately has not gotten by unnoticed.Curator Bio: Addison Rogers is a 
 prominent multi-disciplinary artist\, musician\, and community fixture ba
 sed in Bloomington\, Indiana. Best known as the drummer and co-vocalist f
 or the acclaimed indie-folk outfit Busman's Holiday\, Rogers has spent ov
 er two decades shaping the local cultural landscape. From the band's earl
 y days busking on the B-Line Trail to recording sweeping orchestral album
 s for Indiana's Joyful Noise Recordings\, his creative career is rooted i
 n a deep love for collaborative\, community-driven storytelling. Beyond h
 is work on stage\, Rogers is a champion of local independent media and ar
 ts\, currently serving on the Board of Directors for Bloomington's commun
 ity radio station\, WFHB.Please register below! Advance registration is s
 trongly encouraged and deeply appreciated!
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Dive deep into the archival collections
  of IU Libraries through a screening series of rare and unique archival f
 ilms that center traditionally underrepresented narratives and underrepre
 sented motion-picture practices\, pushing on and expanding the spectrum o
 f what is considered "cinema."</p><p>  In an effort to keep audiences ope
 n-minded and with limited pre-conceptions of these rare works of celluloi
 d\, descriptions of films to be shown will not be shared prior to screeni
 ngs. Join us based on announced themes and the expectation that the works
  you see will fall outside of Hollywood tropes\, outside of mainstream co
 mmercial expectations\, and outside of conventional filmmaking practices.
  Trust us\, you (probably) haven't seen these films before!</p><p><strong
 >September Program</strong>: Working Joy\, curated by Addison Rogers</p><
 p><strong>Program Description</strong>: Working Joy is a concept of takin
 g the necessary break\, the leisure to help get the work done. It's also 
 the necessary work of facilitating good times\, experiences\, true beauty
 . Selections from IULMIA will take us through the process of enjoying lif
 e. Going through the past\, we can see this has always been a practice\, 
 and fortunately has not gotten by unnoticed.</p><p><strong>Curator Bio</s
 trong>: Addison Rogers is a prominent multi-disciplinary artist\, musicia
 n\, and community fixture based in Bloomington\, Indiana. Best known as t
 he drummer and co-vocalist for the acclaimed indie-folk outfit Busman's H
 oliday\, Rogers has spent over two decades shaping the local cultural lan
 dscape. From the band's early days busking on the B-Line Trail to recordi
 ng sweeping orchestral albums for Indiana's Joyful Noise Recordings\, his
  creative career is rooted in a deep love for collaborative\, community-d
 riven storytelling. Beyond his work on stage\, Rogers is a champion of lo
 cal independent media and arts\, currently serving on the Board of Direct
 ors for Bloomington's community radio station\, WFHB.</p><p><strong>Pleas
 e register below! Advance registration is strongly encouraged and deeply 
 appreciated!</strong></p><p><br style="font-weight: 400\;" /><br style="f
 ont-weight: 400\;" /></p>
