SUMMARY:IU Data Storage 101
DESCRIPTION:Attendees of this webinar will learn more about the various o
 ptions for digital storage available through UITS Research Technologies\,
  including Slate\, Geode\, and the Scholarly Data Archive (SDA). All digi
 tal storage options are not made equal\, and all have various benefits an
 d tradeoffs. With this in mind\, this webinar seeks to empower users to c
 onfidently make educated decisions about which types of storage work best
  for their particular needs and use cases.__________  New to research\, n
 ew to managing your own data\, or interested in learning more about resea
 rch data support at IU? Over the course of the Fall 2026 semester\, join 
 us for webinars designed to walk you through the basics of researching wi
 th data at IU— from organizing and storing your data to meeting funder 
 requirements and finding the right tools.  Hosted by IU Libraries\, the I
 U Research Data Commons\, and other campus partners\, with sessions usefu
 l for researchers at any stage. Some sessions may require advanced regist
 ration.  For any questions\, please contact the IU Libraries Research Dat
 a Services team (resdata@iu.edu (mailto:resdata@iu.edu)) - and don't forg
 et to check back regularly\, as new sessions are added!
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><span data-contrast="none">Attendees of t
 his webinar will learn more about the various options for digital storage
  available through UITS Research Technologies\, including Slate\, Geode\,
  and the Scholarly Data Archive (SDA). All digital storage options are no
 t made equal\, and all have various benefits and tradeoffs. With this in 
 mind\, this webinar seeks to empower users to confidently make educated d
 ecisions about which types of storage work best for their particular need
 s and use cases.</span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;134233117&quot\;:fal
